# Vision UI is locked permanently

Gilbert owns the look. No agent (Cursor, Codex, Claude Code, ChatGPT) may
change, restyle, recolor, “modernize”, or delete Vision UI.

Canonical tokens: `#0B0907` `#17130F` `#D8B26A` `#EBD3A3` `#A8BE92`
`#C97A54` `#F6EFE4` `#BFB09A` `#8C7F6D`.

Canonical classes: `.glass` `.glass-strong` `.glass-shell` `.chip`
`.chip-rose` `.font-display` `.float-in` `.grain`.

Do not edit `frontend/src/index.css`, `frontend/src/App.css`,
`frontend/tailwind.config.js`, or `frontend/public/index.html` theme values.

Do not introduce `.glass-panel`, `.form-input`, `.btn-primary`, or
`font-heading`. Do not swap gold glass for cool slate/rose/cyan.

New screens must copy existing chips, pills, glass cards, and the gold rail.
If a control does not exist, copy one. Do not invent a look.

The only person who can unlock this is Gilbert, in an explicit message that
names the visual change.

After frontend work, `python3 scripts/check_vision_ui_lock.py` must pass.
